<title>SWEDEN: Investor posts sharp rise in 9 mo profit.</title>
<headline>Investor posts sharp rise in 9 mo profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial investment company Investor AB reports for the nine months to September 30, 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax items after fin items     11,591  vs  2,140</p>
<p> Total net worth			 73,202  vs 51,225*</p>
<p> Net worth per share (SKR)		366  vs    257*</p>
<p> Market value, main holdings	 53,121  vs 49,275*</p>
<p> Liabilities Saab Auto	 CHARGE 1,040  vs	0</p>
<p> Internal debt to Saab		  5,777  vs  9,583*</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CREDIT  160  vs    446 CHARGE</p>
<p> Consolidated net income Scania '95     0  vs  3,280*</p>
<p> Tax					    227  vs     72</p>
<p> Minorities			  CHARGE  10  vs	4 CHARGE</p>
<p> Consolidated net profit	     11,354  vs  2,064</p>
<p>NOTE -- Swedish industrial investment group Investor AB</p>
<p>*=compared to period to December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
